    "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
    "name": "Identification of the binding sites of the T-cell acute lymphocytic leukemia protein 1 (TAL1)",
    "readme": "This workflow runs a basic ChIP-seq analysis, from raw FASTQ files to peak calling and visualization, as described in the [GTN tutorial](https://gxy.io/GTN:T00143). This workflow has been implemented to predict and analyze the TAL1 binding sites from two mouse cell types.\n\n**Inputs** \n- G1E ChIP paired-end FASTQ files\n- G1E control paired-end FASTQ files\n- Megakaryocyte ChIP paired-end FASTQ files\n- Megakaryocyte control paired-end FASTQ files\n- A BED file containing gene annotations from Mouse genome assembly mm10\n\n**Outputs**\n- Several plots showing the sample correlations, IP strength, and overall peak structure of each of the samples\n- Predicted DNA binding sites \n\n",
    "report": {
        "markdown": "\n# Workflow Execution Report\n\n## Workflow Inputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_inputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow Outputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_outputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow\n```galaxy\nworkflow_display()\n```\n"
    },
